  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    # The transformation appears to consist of removing a border of width floor(N/3)\n    # from the input grid, then taking the resulting inner 5\u00d75 sub\u2011grid.\n    n = len(grid)\n    border = n // 3                # floor(16/3) = 5\n    inner = [row[border:n-border] for row in grid[border:n-border]]\n    # inner is now a 6\u00d76 matrix; we keep only the central 5\u00d75 part.\n    result = [row[:-1] for row in inner[:-1]]\n    return result\n\n# The function follows the discovered rule: it crops the outer\n# floor(N/3) rows and columns, then extracts the central 5\u00d75 region.",
